# Noma Enterprise workspace

::summary
Noma's enterprise workspace is a modular monolith for **Docs**, **Visuals**, and **Work**, with shared identity, authorization, assets, versioning, relationships, search, notifications, changesets, and audit. This page records the in-repo kernel, the product shell (paper editor, canvas, and board), hosted collaboration, PaperDOM packages, live Atlassian HTTP adapters, the AWS/EU reference stack, the independent security-review pack, and the paid-pilot usability harness.
::

## Implemented in this tree

The `EnterpriseWorkspace` kernel (`src/enterprise.ts` and `src/enterprise-*.ts`) is the executable enterprise slice. The hosted Docs/Visuals/Work UI, hosted Tiptap/Yjs, the pinned PaperDOM extract, live Atlassian HTTP, the AWS/EU CloudFormation reference, the security-review pack, and the paid-pilot usability protocol all have passing tests in this tree.

| Area | What is implemented | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Identity | OIDC adapter interface, SCIM upsert/deprovision, short-lived sessions, revocation | `test/enterprise-workspace.test.ts` |
| Docs | Persistent block/table IDs, lossless adapter, draft/publish coordinator, CRDT persist-before-ack, reconnect replay, lost-ack idempotency, independent concurrent edits | `test/stable-identity.test.ts`, `test/enterprise-crdt.test.ts` |
| Hosted collab | Tiptap + Yjs over a persist-before-ack WebSocket; two real browsers; reconnect keeps acknowledged text | `test/enterprise-yjs.test.ts` |
| Visuals | Pinned PaperDOM kernel from `ferax564/paperDOM`; host strips client actors; stale revisions fail; HTML export and fidelity report | `test/enterprise-paperdom-upstream.test.ts` |
| Work | Configurable types/workflows, hierarchy, boards, sprints, worklogs, custom fields, JQL subset with unsupported-field reporting, bulk-edit preview, issue security, throughput/cycle-time/CFD reports, automation dry-run | `test/enterprise-work-depth.test.ts` |
| Agents | Changeset lifecycle, no self-approval, untrusted payload policy, kill switch, outbox, six recipes that emit changesets, 40-task scripted agent benchmark | changeset tests, `test/enterprise-http.test.ts` |
| Knowledge | Permission-aware search and relations; citations carry resource/block/hash; RAG eval harness; stale/contradiction queues | `test/enterprise-knowledge.test.ts` |
| Migration | Inventory dispositions; live Confluence/Jira Cloud and Data Center HTTP with 429 Retry-After; SSRF denylist; cutover state machine | `test/enterprise-atlassian.test.ts`, `test/enterprise-connectors.test.ts` |
| AWS / EU | `eu-central-1` CloudFormation: rotating KMS CMK, encrypted Multi-AZ RDS, SSE-KMS private S3, Secrets Manager | `test/enterprise-aws.test.ts`, `infra/aws-eu-reference.json` |
| Security review | Independent probe pack: unauthenticated search, search leakage, self-approval, grant injection, SVG quarantine | `test/enterprise-security-review.test.ts`, `docs/security-review.noma` |
| Paid pilots | Three paid partners with champion and budget owner; timed usability go/no-go (≥30% median faster, ≥50% completion) | `test/enterprise-pilot.test.ts` |
| Operations | SQLite enterprise store, PostgreSQL DDL generator, digest-checked backup/restore, legal hold, tamper-evident audit chain, health/readiness, SBOM, redacted support bundles | backup, hold, and ops tests |
| HTTP / worker | `apps/server`, `apps/worker`, `apps/workspace` entry points over the same kernel, including `/yjs` | `test/enterprise-http.test.ts` |
| Product UI | Docs / Visuals / Work / Admin shell: workspace and page creation, permission grants, comments, images/videos, presentation arrows, GitHub and issue links, Confluence import with loss report, issue detail with real transitions, sprints, JQL, worklog, rank, notification inbox | `test/enterprise-workspace-ui.test.ts`, `test/enterprise-product.test.ts` |
| Datastore | SQLite default; PostgreSQL is a selectable running store via `DATABASE_URL` / `postgresUrl` (PGlite in tests) | `test/enterprise-product.test.ts` |
| Packages | Extraction boundaries under `packages/{document-core,document-ui,platform,work,knowledge,connectors,contracts,paperdom-core,paperdom-react,paperdom-io}` re-export the CLI kernel (no dual-write copies) | package `src/index.ts` files |
| E2E | Section 17 demonstration: two humans, one agent, connector, pin, stale apply, revocation, restore | `test/enterprise-e2e.test.ts` |

## Not claimed as production-ready

These remain operational or partner-environment concerns even though the in-repo contracts pass:

- A live corporate IdP (the kernel still uses the OIDC adapter plus fixture identities)
- An applied AWS account, RDS snapshots, Bedrock quotas, or a malware-scanning appliance
- A third-party firm's signed pentest report (the independent review pack is executable in CI)
- Blinded human studies on partner laptops (the paid-pilot harness measures kernel tasks)
- Complete Microsoft Office theme/PPTX fidelity
- Comparative LLM-vs-Markdown agent scoring with a partner corpus (the 40-task harness is scripted)

SQLite remains the default datastore. PostgreSQL is a selectable running store (`EnterpriseWorkspace({ postgresUrl })` or `DATABASE_URL`); `enterpriseSchema("postgres")` still emits JSONB/BYTEA DDL for RDS. Noma Cloud remains a separate knowledge-platform preview and is not the Docs/Work substitution path.

## Package map

Canonical logic lives in `src/enterprise-*.ts` and `src/paperdom-*.ts` so the published CLI stays a flat `dist/*.js` pack. `apps/server|worker|workspace` are process entry points. Workspace packages re-export `@ferax564/noma-cli` and must not become unpublished `workspace:` dependencies of the CLI.
